    "message": "Schedule staff role changes instead of crashing\n\nScheduling set_staff_role read the validated parameters as a model,\nbut they are a plain dict there, so approving the program raised\nAttributeError before the Branch existed (#72). Once that passed, the\nEffectProgram state check rejected the start event because the\noperator was missing from its event-type table.\n\nRead the skills from the dict and register the operator's start event.\nThe role change now applies, and the intervention test no longer\nexpects failure.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
